{"id":"2693d6bd81a90afb","group":"93","path":"93/93-thm-soundness.md","title":"Soundness Theorem","display":"Soundness Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Algebraizable Logics","book_abbrev":"93","label":"93-thm-soundness","aliases":["93-thm-soundness"],"display":"Soundness Theorem","depends_on":["[[93-df-proof]]","[[93-df-semantic-consequence]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"93"},{"key":"label","html":"93-thm-soundness"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>93-thm-soundness</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"Soundness Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"4e0a05ab276dc277\" href=\"?note=4e0a05ab276dc277\" title=\"93-df-proof\">93-df-proof</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"8b587d680bb02f51\" href=\"?note=8b587d680bb02f51\" title=\"93-df-semantic-consequence\">93-df-semantic-consequence</a></span></div>"}],"html":"<h1 id=\"thm-soundness-—-Soundness-Theorem\">thm-soundness — Soundness Theorem</h1>\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal L\">\\(\\mathcal L\\)</span> is a first-order language, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F=\\mathrm{FOFml}_{93}(\\mathcal L)\">\\(F=\\mathrm{FOFml}_{93}(\\mathcal L)\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Calc}_{93}(\\mathcal P;F)\">\\(\\mathrm{Calc}_{93}(\\mathcal P;F)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Seq}(F)\">\\(\\mathrm{Seq}(F)\\)</span> is the finite-sequence set used by <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"4e0a05ab276dc277\" href=\"?note=4e0a05ab276dc277\" title=\"93-df-proof\">93-df-proof</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal K\\subseteq\\operatorname{FOStr}_{93}(\\mathcal L)\">\\(\\mathcal K\\subseteq\\operatorname{FOStr}_{93}(\\mathcal L)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\models_{\\mathcal K,\\mathcal L}\">\\(\\models_{\\mathcal K,\\mathcal L}\\)</span> is the semantic consequence relation of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"8b587d680bb02f51\" href=\"?note=8b587d680bb02f51\" title=\"93-df-semantic-consequence\">93-df-semantic-consequence</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Proof}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{Proof}_{93}\\)</span> is the proof predicate of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"4e0a05ab276dc277\" href=\"?note=4e0a05ab276dc277\" title=\"93-df-proof\">93-df-proof</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Rules}_{\\mathcal P}\">\\(\\mathrm{Rules}_{\\mathcal P}\\)</span> is the rule family carried by the displayed calculus.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}soundness}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Calc}_{93}(\\mathcal P;F)\\land F=\\mathrm{FOFml}_{93}(\\mathcal L)\n\\land\\mathcal K\\subseteq\\operatorname{FOStr}_{93}(\\mathcal L)\n\\land\\forall\\alpha\\in\\mathrm{Ax}_{\\mathcal P}\\;\n(\\varnothing\\models_{\\mathcal K,\\mathcal L}\\alpha)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall R\\in\\mathrm{Rules}_{\\mathcal P}\\;\\forall q\\in\\mathrm{Seq}(F)\\;\\forall\\chi\\in F\\;\n\\bigl(\\langle q,\\chi\\rangle\\in R\\to\n\\operatorname{ran}(q)\\models_{\\mathcal K,\\mathcal L}\\chi\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\forall\\Gamma\\subseteq F\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in F\\;\\Bigl(\n\\exists p\\;\\mathrm{Proof}_{93}(p,\\varphi,\\mathcal P,\\Gamma)\n\\to\\Gamma\\models_{\\mathcal K,\\mathcal L}\\varphi\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}soundness}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Calc}_{93}(\\mathcal P;F)\\land F=\\mathrm{FOFml}_{93}(\\mathcal L)\n\\land\\mathcal K\\subseteq\\operatorname{FOStr}_{93}(\\mathcal L)\n\\land\\forall\\alpha\\in\\mathrm{Ax}_{\\mathcal P}\\;\n(\\varnothing\\models_{\\mathcal K,\\mathcal L}\\alpha)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall R\\in\\mathrm{Rules}_{\\mathcal P}\\;\\forall q\\in\\mathrm{Seq}(F)\\;\\forall\\chi\\in F\\;\n\\bigl(\\langle q,\\chi\\rangle\\in R\\to\n\\operatorname{ran}(q)\\models_{\\mathcal K,\\mathcal L}\\chi\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\forall\\Gamma\\subseteq F\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in F\\;\\Bigl(\n\\exists p\\;\\mathrm{Proof}_{93}(p,\\varphi,\\mathcal P,\\Gamma)\n\\to\\Gamma\\models_{\\mathcal K,\\mathcal L}\\varphi\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>Soundness follows by induction on proof length. Rule soundness is stated as semantic consequence from the rule's finite premise sequence, so no unsupported helper predicates remain.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"thm-soundness-—-Soundness-Theorem","text":"thm-soundness — Soundness Theorem","level":1},{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-proof","status":"resolved","id":"4e0a05ab276dc277","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-proof]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-semantic-consequence","status":"resolved","id":"8b587d680bb02f51","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-semantic-consequence]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-proof","status":"resolved","id":"4e0a05ab276dc277","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Seq}(F)$ is the finite-sequence set used by [[93-df-proof]].","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-semantic-consequence","status":"resolved","id":"8b587d680bb02f51","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathcal K\\subseteq\\operatorname{FOStr}_{93}(\\mathcal L)$ and $\\models_{\\mathcal K,\\mathcal L}$ is the semantic consequence relation of [[93-df-semantic-consequence]].","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-proof","status":"resolved","id":"4e0a05ab276dc277","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Proof}_{93}$ is the proof predicate of [[93-df-proof]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathcal L","display":false},{"tex":"F=\\mathrm{FOFml}_{93}(\\mathcal L)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Calc}_{93}(\\mathcal P;F)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Seq}(F)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal K\\subseteq\\operatorname{FOStr}_{93}(\\mathcal L)","display":false},{"tex":"\\models_{\\mathcal K,\\mathcal L}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Proof}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Rules}_{\\mathcal P}","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}soundness}\\vdash{}&\n\\mathrm{Calc}_{93}(\\mathcal P;F)\\land F=\\mathrm{FOFml}_{93}(\\mathcal L)\n\\land\\mathcal K\\subseteq\\operatorname{FOStr}_{93}(\\mathcal L)\n\\land\\forall\\alpha\\in\\mathrm{Ax}_{\\mathcal P}\\;\n(\\varnothing\\models_{\\mathcal K,\\mathcal L}\\alpha)\\\\\n&\\land\\forall R\\in\\mathrm{Rules}_{\\mathcal P}\\;\\forall q\\in\\mathrm{Seq}(F)\\;\\forall\\chi\\in F\\;\n\\bigl(\\langle q,\\chi\\rangle\\in R\\to\n\\operatorname{ran}(q)\\models_{\\mathcal K,\\mathcal L}\\chi\\bigr)\\\\\n&\\to\\forall\\Gamma\\subseteq F\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in F\\;\\Bigl(\n\\exists p\\;\\mathrm{Proof}_{93}(p,\\varphi,\\mathcal P,\\Gamma)\n\\to\\Gamma\\models_{\\mathcal K,\\mathcal L}\\varphi\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true}],"bytes":1684,"backlinks":[],"outgoing":["4e0a05ab276dc277","8b587d680bb02f51"]}